MAKE(1)                     User Commands                    MAKE(1)

NAME
    make - maintain program dependencies

SYNOPSIS
    make [--posix] [-C path] [-f makefile] [-j num] [-ehiknpqrsSt]
         [macro=value...] [target...]

DESCRIPTION
    make reads the rules in Makefile or makefile, or in the files named with
    -f, and rebuilds each named target whose prerequisites are newer than
    it by running the commands of its rule with /bin/sh. Without a target
    the first target of the first file is built.

OPTIONS
    --posix      disable the extensions; must be the first option
    -C path      change to path before reading the makefile
    -e           let environment variables override makefile macros
    -f makefile  read makefile instead of Makefile; - is standard input
    -h           print the usage
    -i           ignore errors from commands
    -j num       accepted; commands run one at a time
    -k           continue with other targets after an error
    -n           print commands without running them
    -p           print the macros and rules
    -q           exit 0 when the targets are up to date, 1 otherwise
    -r           do not use the built-in rules
    -s           do not print commands
    -S           stop at the first error (default)
    -t           touch the targets instead of building them

EXTENSIONS
    Double colon rules; ifdef, ifndef, ifeq, ifneq, else, endif; archive
    members lib.a(member.o); := assignments; chained inference rules;
    wildcards in target rules; $< and $* in target rules; a backslash
    escaping #; macros and targets mixed on the command line. The .POSIX
    target, the --posix option and the environment variable
    PDPMAKE_POSIXLY_CORRECT disable them.

EXAMPLES
    make
    make -n clean
    make -f build.mk CC=cc all

SEE ALSO
    sh(1), touch(1), ar(1)
